RV32IM SoC integration test image
=================================

Load tb/test_all.hex into cpu_rv32im_top using HEX_FILE="tb/test_all.hex".
Each HEX line is one 32-bit instruction, loaded at the matching word address.
The addresses below are byte addresses; the first instruction starts at 0x00000000.

GPIO result:
  0x00000055 = PASS (all checks reached)
  0x000000EE = FAIL (a branch detected an incorrect result)
The program writes the signature to MMIO address 0x80000000 and then parks.
Data RAM test location is byte address 0x00000100 (word index 64).

Coverage
--------
  ALU: ADD, SUB, AND, OR, XOR, SLT, SLTU.
  Forwarding: back-to-back dependent ADDI/ADD operations.
  Load-use: LW followed immediately by an instruction consuming its result.
  Branches: taken BEQ, not-taken BEQ, and BNE result checks.
  Jumps: JAL and JALR redirect and link-address checks.
  DMEM: SW followed by LW; loaded value is then consumed by ADD.
  RV32M: MUL, DIV, and REM with expected results 120, 3, and 2.
  GPIO MMIO: PASS/FAIL signature store.

Address    Machine code  Instruction / purpose
--------   ------------  ---------------------
00000000   01400093      addi x1,x0,20              ; operand A
00000004   00600113      addi x2,x0,6               ; operand B
00000008   002081b3      add x3,x1,x2               ; x3 = 26 (forwarding)
0000000c   01a00213      addi x4,x0,26              ; expected value
00000010   0c419c63      bne x3,x4,fail             ; ADD check
00000014   402082b3      sub x5,x1,x2               ; x5 = 14
00000018   00e00213      addi x4,x0,14
0000001c   0c429663      bne x5,x4,fail             ; SUB check
00000020   0020f333      and x6,x1,x2               ; x6 = 4
00000024   00400213      addi x4,x0,4
00000028   0c431063      bne x6,x4,fail             ; AND check
0000002c   0020e3b3      or x7,x1,x2                ; x7 = 22
00000030   01600213      addi x4,x0,22
00000034   0a439a63      bne x7,x4,fail             ; OR check
00000038   0020c433      xor x8,x1,x2               ; x8 = 18
0000003c   01200213      addi x4,x0,18
00000040   0a441463      bne x8,x4,fail             ; XOR check
00000044   001124b3      slt x9,x2,x1               ; x9 = 1 (signed 6 < 20)
00000048   00100213      addi x4,x0,1
0000004c   08449e63      bne x9,x4,fail             ; SLT check
00000050   00113533      sltu x10,x2,x1             ; x10 = 1 (unsigned 6 < 20)
00000054   08451a63      bne x10,x4,fail            ; SLTU check
00000058   00300593      addi x11,x0,3              ; forwarding chain starts
0000005c   00458613      addi x12,x11,4             ; x12 = 7
00000060   00b606b3      add x13,x12,x11            ; x13 = 10
00000064   00a00213      addi x4,x0,10
00000068   08469063      bne x13,x4,fail            ; dependent ALU check
0000006c   10000713      addi x14,x0,256            ; RAM byte address 0x100
00000070   00d72023      sw x13,0(x14)              ; store 10 to RAM
00000074   00072783      lw x15,0(x14)              ; read it back
00000078   00178833      add x16,x15,x1             ; load-use dependency; x16 = 30
0000007c   01e00213      addi x4,x0,30
00000080   06481463      bne x16,x4,fail            ; load-use and RAM check
00000084   00318463      beq x3,x3,branch_taken_ok   ; must take branch
00000088   0600006f      jal x0,fail                ; fail if branch was not taken
0000008c   04418e63      beq x3,x4,fail             ; must not take: 26 != 30
00000090   0080036f      jal x6,jal_ok               ; x6 receives link 0x94
00000094   0540006f      jal x0,fail                ; fail if JAL did not redirect
00000098   09400213      addi x4,x0,148             ; expected JAL link address
0000009c   04431663      bne x6,x4,fail             ; verify JAL link
000000a0   0ac00893      addi x17,x0,172            ; absolute JALR target 0xAC
000000a4   000883e7      jalr x7,0(x17)              ; x7 receives link 0xA8
000000a8   0400006f      jal x0,fail                ; fail if JALR did not redirect
000000ac   0a800213      addi x4,x0,168             ; expected JALR link address
000000b0   02439c63      bne x7,x4,fail             ; verify JALR link
000000b4   02208933      mul x18,x1,x2              ; x18 = 120
000000b8   07800213      addi x4,x0,120
000000bc   02491663      bne x18,x4,fail            ; MUL check
000000c0   0220c9b3      div x19,x1,x2              ; x19 = 3
000000c4   00300213      addi x4,x0,3
000000c8   02499063      bne x19,x4,fail            ; DIV check
000000cc   0220ea33      rem x20,x1,x2              ; x20 = 2
000000d0   00200213      addi x4,x0,2
000000d4   004a1a63      bne x20,x4,fail            ; REM check
000000d8   80000ab7      lui x21,0x80000            ; GPIO base = 0x80000000
000000dc   05500b13      addi x22,x0,0x55           ; PASS signature
000000e0   016aa023      sw x22,0(x21)              ; write PASS to GPIO
000000e4   0100006f      jal x0,done                ; skip FAIL handler
000000e8   80000ab7      lui x21,0x80000            ; fail handler: GPIO base
000000ec   0ee00b13      addi x22,x0,0xEE           ; FAIL signature
000000f0   016aa023      sw x22,0(x21)              ; write FAIL to GPIO
000000f4   0000006f      jal x0,done                ; park forever

Notes
-----
JAL/JALR link checks require the decoder to select PC+4 as the writeback source.
GPIO stores are full-word SWs, matching the current top-level GPIO register.
